If it doesn't say aircraft on it somewhere, it isn't legal in a[ certific]ated aircraft. Be careful you don't spend tons of time cutting and fitting something that your mechanic then has a fit about.
Boeing supposedly has some honeycomb material available surplus that is legal aircraft grade, that a friend of mine thinks might make good floorboards.
